\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 The nature of physics, and especially the nature of universes, should only be taught and discussed in amusement parks. There is a train of philosophical thought that postulates that\'92s why they were invented in the first place. A perception of truth first requires the derangement of the senses, a re-patching of the wires of sequential thought, a scattering of the sense of self via kinetics on the edge of casualty, a scrambling of the order of belief, prejudice, logic, expectation, and little itches that defy all attempts to scratch them away.\
Words are the problem, and we don\'92t have the un-words, which makes the following narration somewhat problematic. \'93Ascension\'94 implies up to somewhere, whereas the Dawkins became everywhere and nowhere for all points of non-time. \'93The council met\'94 is a poor approximation of an eternally ongoing process of not-one, not-many being-ness-es\'85 Damn: \'93eternal\'94 is inaccurate as well.\
Look, let\'92s just step back a poofteenth of a picosecond, to the fulcrum of a moment between when a universe is happily expanding, minding its own business and when it no longer has business to mind because it has been snuffed into untimely, anti-spatial non-existence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
