\f1\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22 And that\'92s when Sarah\'92s waters broke.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 The three of the Seven Sages who weren\'92t pursuing personal projects due to artistic differences were ecstatic to witness the ascension of the Dawkins (
\f3\i He\'92s the One!
\f0\i0 ). It was as \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 wondrous as it was indescribable\'97a Vision Splendid of Little Clinton rising from Mother Sarah\'92s arms, glowing like a cherub-shaped night-light, rising regally, as graceful as a dirigible, his penile tether dangling below his chubby bottom, which was as squidgy as a soft jelly-baby.\
The Elvi bowed their heads and praised the Holy Momma.\
Dr Ortolan took one last glance at his watch.\
Chip and Johnny were surprised even a red button would do 
\f3\i that
\f0\i0 .\
Eloise wondered how her defensive weapons had failed.\
Alexander saw an alien abduction\'97his son being stolen before his eyes.\
Chanta saw Sarah and Little Clinton in an aura of light and love, and heard the lyrics of a song about it.\
The Jones clones saw a baby \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
exploding in a burning ring of fire.\
In the end, the three of the Seven Sages\'97who weren\'92t pursuing personal projects due to artistic differences\'97were caught on the prophetic hop as all Creation snuffed itself out. Who would have guessed that the ascent of a single being would cost the gas of a whole universe\'85\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0  possibly something to do with the conservation of energy and all that buzzkill hard-science stuff. Although, if he\'92d been spared, Chilo would have claimed he\'92d seen it coming.\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22 \'93Welcome, Multi-Universal entirety of Little Clinton Dawkins,\'94 said a non-voice in a strange accent that the Multi-Universal entirety of Little Clinton Dawkins realised was strange mostly because the speaker wasn\'92t using English.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 \'93Well, this is unexpected,\'94 the \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Multi-Universal (or \'93MU\'94) \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
entirety of Little Clinton Dawkins answered in the same language.\
\'93You are invited to a Council Meeting of Ascendency,\'94 the non-voice said without actually saying anything.\
\'93Ascendency?\'94\
\'93Yes, we all hate it too, but there you are. Allow a fancy word to come from the mouths of sporting commentators and it pretty much becomes indelible. Whatever you wish to call it, we already understand. Oh, and there will be Devonshire Tea.\'94\
\'93Really?\'94\
The other Being chortled. \'93I make a joke. Devonshire Tea is in all things as all things are in the tea leaves.\'94\
\'93I see,\'94 Mu Dawkins said.\
\'93Yes, well, you\'92ll soon lose the tics of sensory-oriented language,\'94 the Being said.\
Mu Dawkins found himself with the Council, which possibly was as it has always been. Or is always being.\
\'93Welcome Mu Dawkins,\'94 said a different non-voice from everywhere. \'93Now tell us. What will you create?\'94\
\'93Create?\'94 Even as ascendant as Mu Dawkins was or is, Mu Dawkins was or is confused by that.\
\'93Yes, create! Your first duty as a multi-universal entirety is to replace the one you consumed into your Being.\'94\
\'93What? I destroyed\'97\'94\
\'93\'97Consumed\'97\'94\
\'93A whole universe.\'94\
The non-voice hummed to itself for a few moments. \'93Ah. Usually ascendency requires full knowledge, including the knowledge of the consequences.\'94\
\'93That can\'92t possibly be right,\'94 Mu Dawkins objected.\
\'93You are in error, Mu Dawkins. It is, in fact, not possibly wrong. As we speak is right.\'94 \
\'93But\'85 all gone? Mother? Uncle Chanta?\'94\
\'93It is good that you revere those who you sacrificed,\'94 a new non-voice kept uttering.\
\'93So, be telling us,\'94\'97yet another\'97\'93What will you create?\'94\
\'93Ah, perhaps we should speak of the Caveats.\'94\'97another.\
\'93Well, there is the User\'92s Guide and the Real Universe Estate Act\'85\'94\
\'93Yes, you can be looking them up later, but the main ones are: no dinosaurs stomping about in the time of humans; no multi-breasted women; no aliens or alien abduction myths; no polka; no mac-and-cheese, and\'97this is an absolute deal-breaker\'97no super heroes.\'94\
\'93No super heroes?\'94\
\'93We are not liking your tone, Mu Dawkins. You are Ascendant and we expect you to be acting like it.\'94\
Yet another non-voice\'97\'93To be clear, we mean no super heroes in\'97but not limited to\'97comics, cartoons, movies, advertising, themed weddings, kink parties\'85\'94\
\'93Yes, yes, yes\'97the list goes on. Trust those of us who have already dabbled, and regretted it. If you create just one super hero\'97they infest your whole entertainment industry and you can never get them out.\'94\
\'93I rather think that if Mu Dawkins wishes to create their universe with super heroes, they should be allowed\'97\'94\
\'93This matter was already settled millions of years away.\'94\
Mu Dawkins found a space to interject. \'93Create? But I spent my whole life debunking Creation myths.\'94\
\'93Come, now, Mu Dawkins, we\'92re here now and forever, and it is your duty to replace the universe you consumed.\'94\
\'93I won\'92t do it. I won\'92t play God to a fresh universe.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22 Mu Dawkins sulked for an interminable tract of un-time, obstinately refusing  to create anything, which stuck in the craws of the other white-bearded, multi-limbed, or diversely-headed ascendants.\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 And there was a huge vacuum where the universe that had given its life to spawn Mu Dawkins had been.\
Property developers were getting impatient.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22 Mu Dawkins filled their infinite days with culture and hobbies. They went to the opera and attended performances of Vaughan Williams; they went for long walks, watched Monty Python and listened to 
\f3\i The Hitchhiker\'92s Guide to the Galaxy
\f0\i0  on a radio. They acquired fresh white linen, entertained angels, and finally read Heidegger. Then they learned to play cricket.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 On the seventh day of infinite time, they rested\'97with fresh white linen and entertaining angels. On the eighth day they were summoned to a Council Meeting of Ascendency and immediately it was around Mu Dawkins, even as they were dressed in nothing but bedsheets.\
\'93Behold what we have wrought in the abyss you left like a hole in the cosmic fly-screen,\'94 a non-voice intoned. Was it non-voice Mu Dawkins had heard from before? They weren\'92t sure.\
What was once a hole in the cosmic fly-screen was suddenly all around them, or they had been cast into it. They coughed, choking on rough and rank fibres that smelled like neglected laundry.\
The same non-voice continued. \'93We found a solution to our missing socks problem, and cast them all into the abyss that should be the manifestation of your Creation.\'94\
Mu Dawkins coughed again.\
\'93You have found your socks; now you can wear them.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22 Mu Dawkins relented and promised they would repair their hole in the cosmic fly-screen.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 Creating a whole new universe was an overwhelming responsibility. Meddling in what Mu Dawkins knew was the process of evolution was fraught. How could one being presume to alter the cumulative effects of uncountable tiny pivots in events? Even with the best of intentions, billionaires who founded institutions to solve the world\'92s greatest ills invariably made things worse, because they couldn\'92t leave their egos out of their endeavours. How much more damage could a being with a god-complex inflict upon a disempowered universe?\
Still, it wasn\'92t as if naturally evolved universes didn\'92t come with pain and tragedy. Mu Dawkins reflected on the universe that had borne them, the one they had allegedly made their first meal of. It was full of atrocities like the Crusades; the \cf3 Wanggongchang Explosion; the \cf2 Spanish Inquisition that no one expected; the Taiping Rebellion; COVID-19; the Tenerife airport disaster; the Mongol conquests; indiscriminate outsourcing; Japanese war crimes; the CIA, KGB, FSB and Mossad; the European colonisation of \'93new\'94 worlds; space shuttle disasters; the Dungan revolt; the wars on terror, drugs and gender reassignment; the Great Data Centre Fires; and big oil, big tobacco, big pharma, big fast food, and big K-pop.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 But there was the trap: who was anyone to play watchmaker of a new universe? It would be no more than a vast form of outsider art, imbued with the artist\'92s prejudices and enlightenments, grievances and graces, with personal tastes mistaken for universal truths, and finite intelligence attempting to encompass infinite possibilities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22  Mu Dawkins called a \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Council Meeting of Ascendency and, immediately, they were in it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 \'93Put it back,\'94 Mu Dawkins said. \'93Put my old universe back, just the way it was.\'94\
There was much laughter, as if a puppy had done something especially stupid and endearing.\
\'93It is not possible. You consumed it.\'94\
\'93Well, start it again, let it re-evolve.\'94\
\'93It will contain you again. The outcome will be the same.\'94\
\'93Are you sure? I mean\'85 quantum uncertainty and all that\'85\'94\
There was silence.\
An uncountable number of awarenesses occupying all of time and space cleared their throats and scratched their earlobes.\
A non-voice\'97\'93We know not for sure.\'94\
\'93I see.\'94\
\'93But there is a possibility, if not a probability of a possibility, that it will contain you again.\'94\
Mu Dawkins dwelled on that for a long no-time. \'93What if we restarted it, let it evolve as it will, but made minimal tweaks?\'94\
The non-voice\'97\'93It is already within your power to do so.\'94 \
A different non-voice\'97\'93But we must caution you to make your interventions early. Attempts to compensate and twiddle outcomes later tend to result in catastrophic systemic consequences.\'94\
Mu Dawkins felt the effects of their smiling across all space and time. \'93Okay, let\'92s do it. But, this is my first time; I\'92m sure I\'92ll need some help.\'94\
\'93That is what we are here for.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Mu Dawkins prevaricated; they hedged, they second-guessed, they reconsidered. Yet they would have to do something\'97just restarting that decrepit, defective universe was no option. But how much intervention would hit the Goldilocks zone of twiddling? Mu Dawkins leaned towards too little, to letting evolution do more of the work, but they still wanted to make enough of a change to make enough of a difference. There was much of it that Mu Dawkins could not meddle in, despite their compassion for the reboot of the universe that had spawned them. There would still be plagues, floods, fires, earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, amusement park accidents, and erectile dysfunction. There would till be nuclear weapons and fidget-spinners, yodelling and coffee pods, Pok\'e9mon and flash mobs.\
In the meantime, the missing sock conglomerate that festered where their consumed universe used to be was becoming particularly fetid and was offending the neighbours. Still, Mu Dawkins had a half-billion-year window in which they had to decide.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 They ran simulations until Mu Dawkins realised that even those caused real suffering in the stuff of which they were made. Eventually they placed their fingerprints delicately upon the evolutionary scales, hoping they had not overtipped them.\
None of the interventions guaranteed the desired outcomes, but Mu Dawkins remained resolute that they would force nothing through the caprice of Creationism.\
The outcomes were modest: that Sarah should be born free of sarcoglycanopathy; that Chanta should live the happy life of a cleaning contractor, supported by his beautiful and capable partner who was a descendant of Sarah; that Douglas Adams should not die so young; and that the original Elvis\'85\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f0\fs22 This is where it could be said that Mu Dawkins exceeded the bounds of their original, modest interventionism.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0\fs22 The Elvis of Mu Dawkins\'92 reboot fares rather better than most. He grows up in dignity and relative comfort, never loses his childhood home; he is well-educated, learns to read music and understand nutrition; he grows out of his mother fixation; he gets along with Frank Sinatra; he never fears being a father; he is never exploited by avaricious management; Catholics never report him to the FBI director (Mu Dawkins was initially tempted to dispense with Catholics and the FBI). Fortuitously, the Estonian word for 
\f3\i pelvis
\f0\i0  (
\f3\i vaagnaluu
\f0\i0 ) does not rhyme with his name. Young Elvis grows healthy and loved, though not so famous and rich, but that yields its own rewards: souvenir-hungry mobs never strip him naked and steal his clothes, and he never feels the need to hide away in a mansion for the sake of safety. He receives and takes good medical advice; he is never conscripted. He lives as he wishes, devoting his life to the things he love most: singing and shakin\'92 that thing, and pulling over speeding drivers, lecturing them, and giving them tickets to which he duly affixes his autograph. This Elvis lives well into his nineties until his final Vegas show at the Kadriorg 
\f3\i Pension\'e4ride Mugavusmaja Lugupeetud Vanuritele
\f0\i0  where, during a particularly vigorous performance of 
\f3\i Jail House Rock
\f0\i0 , he throws his hip so far, it cracks.\
Mu Dawkins watches with a pang of sympathy as their Elvis passes somewhat ignominiously, but is there such a thing as a good way to die? This Elvis would\'92ve fallen from the stage, except for an improbable conjunction between a microphone stand and a tangle of industrially sturdy gold chains that hangs from his neck and adorned his manly nonagenarian chest. Tragically, his chains tangles around the microphone stand, and that was almost that. He manages one last, gurgling utterance of 
\f3\i Thank you very much
\f0\i0 . He passes before his cape settles, and receives a standing ovation, from those residents of the 
\f3\i Pension\'e4ride Mugavusmaja
\f0\i0  who are still able to get out of their chairs. Rhinestones and sequins reflect a starry night sky on the ceiling and walls.\
Alert readers may now be asking 
\f3\i Where the hell is Kadriorg
\f0\i0 ? 
\f3\i And what the hell is a Pension\'e4ride Mugavusmaja?
\f0\i0  To which we must admit, we\'92ve been a bit coy about certain details regarding this happy Elvis in this rebooted universe.\
The first is, Elvis Aaron Presley was not his name.\
\'92Twas Elvei Aaron Preestriheinamaa.\
The second is\'85\
Yep. The Elvis of this world was Estonian.
